# The committed state of this fixture is a clean Next.js 16 app with Tailwind v4
# and deliberately no components.json, which is the single condition
# scripts/assert-init-refuses.mjs exists to test. Nothing generated belongs in
# it.
#
# next-env.d.ts is written by `next build`, and it references types under
# .next/, so its committed content would describe whichever build last ran here.
# apps/web and apps/docs track theirs because they are shipped applications and
# that is the Next.js convention. A fixture is not, for the same reason
# apps/fixture-next16/.gitignore gives: anyone who builds locally to debug
# something is then one `git add -A` away from committing generated output, and
# it reads as ordinary work in review.
#
# assert-init-refuses.mjs hashes this directory from the filesystem rather than
# from git, so ignoring a file here does not narrow what it checks.
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo
